{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/nearestNeighborTour(weight:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"nearestNeighborTour","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Walks\/documentation\/Walks\/Cycle","text":"Cycle","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">? ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdditiveArithmetic","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tours read the simple graph: self-loops are ignored, and each pair of vertices is joined by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its lightest edge (the earliest position on ties), which is the edge the returned ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cycle"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"uses, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cycle.weight(weight)"},{"text":" is the tour’s length. nil below three vertices, before any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other check. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"text":" is called once per non-loop edge, in position order, before any work.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"No approximation guarantee in general; within ½(⌈log₂ n⌉ + 1) of the shortest tour when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the weights satisfy the triangle inequality (Rosenkrantz, Stearns and Lewis, “An analysis","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of several heuristics for the traveling salesman problem”, SIAM Journal on Computing 6,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1977).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The graph is complete (every pair of distinct vertices joined); no weight","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is NaN or infinite.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n²) after O(n + m) to read the edges and weights.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Complexity"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The nearest-neighbour tour from the first vertex (NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"greedy_tsp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", JGraphT","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NearestNeighborHeuristicTSP(first)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whose default starts at a random vertex): repeatedly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the nearest unvisited vertex, the first in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order on ties, then back to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"start. LEMON’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"NearestNeighborTsp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shares the name only: it starts from the lightest edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and grows the path at both ends, a different procedure and tour.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/nearestneighbortour(weight:)"]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5ToursE19nearestNeighborTour6weight5Walks5CycleVy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGSgqd__ANXE_ts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"name":"Tours","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"NearestNeighbor.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tours\/NearestNeighbor.swift#L70"},"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"nearestNeighborTour","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind"